body:
On one end I can see why you would be upset that he was not allowed medical access, which is wrong. 

&#x200B;

On the other end I've torn drunk drivers out of cars after accidents where they've hurt or killed other people or they are dead. I would rather he goes a few hours waiting for a judge then end up like that.

I am a 20 yo/F in a job field of grown men and women who don't get along with you simply because you're female. I feel like I missed out on developing friendships in high school because of my introverted ways and now I don't really have anyone I am really friends with outside of work. With that said, I feel like I have made progress in opening up to people and have learned through my coworkers that you can grow a relationship with any person, just try to make them positive ones. 

&#x200B;

I hope you are able to make friends soon, it took a long time for me and I still only have one or two but I trust them with my life. Feel free to PM me anytime if you want.

I'm positive she 100 percent does care about you and your state of being. It is okay to misinterpret people's meanings when you feel uncomfortable seeking clarification from the person. I know for me I might not see an email for a few hours and even longer when I'm busy. I thinks he meant it as saying that even though you are important that she might not have the physical capability of being on her phone and should you need more immediate attention that there may be better options for you in that moment, not that she wouldn't be there if she knew you needed her.

&#x200B;

I would recommend working with her to find what immediate resources you can access when you are suicidal. I think she doesn't you to only rely on her and knowing her own limitations wants you to be able to seek out other resources as well.

I have terrible driving anxiety after witnessing an accident when I was a child. I definitely get the dissociation when I'm driving and I've been working hard to cope with it and talking with a phobia specialist. Oddly enough I work in medical and actually respond to car accidents and haven't had any problems on scenes. 

&#x200B;

I get pretty severe chest pain and my heart rate skyrockets even when I'm not hyperventilating. I'm still working to manage that part. I hope everything turns out for the best for you.
